    "extraction_notes": [
      "Multi-part datasheet covering 2SC5658/2SC4617EB/2SC4617/2SC4081UB/2SC4081/2SC2412K with shared electrical characteristics. 2SC2412KT146R is 2SC2412K in SOT-346 (SMT3) with T146 taping code, hFE rank QRS (120-560), marking B (p. 1 packaging specifications; p. 2 hFE rank table).",
      "Curves digitized programmatically from a 300 dpi render with gridline-based axis calibration on both axes of every figure; the 25 degC curve was selected from each multi-temperature family using the legend callout order printed in the figure.",
      "Fig. 3 hFE 25 degC curve digitized over 1-70 mA only: above roughly 100 mA the four temperature curves converge and cross during gain rolloff and cannot be attributed unambiguously, so those points are omitted.",
      "Table typical fT is 180 MHz at IE = -2 mA while the digitized fig. 8 curve reads about 198 MHz at 2 mA; table typical Cob is 2.0 pF at VCB = 12 V while the digitized fig. 9 Cob curve reads about 1.68 pF at 12 V. Both sources are retained as published; the specs.ft and specs.cobo fields carry the guaranteed characterization table rows.",
      "Fig. 8 x axis uses ROHM's negative emitter current convention (current flowing out of the emitter of an NPN); curve points and the cibo/ft condition strings record magnitudes in SI units.",
      "Saturation curves (fig. 5 and fig. 7) are at forced beta IC/IB = 10, pulsed; the guaranteed VCE(sat) table row (max 400 mV) is at IC = 50 mA, IB = 5 mA, also IC/IB = 10. VBE(sat) is not tabulated, so the table saturation row carries vbe_sat = null.",
      "Additional absolute maximum ratings on p. 2 not representable in the specs schema: VCBO 60 V, VEBO 7 V, IC 150 mA (ICP 200 mA pulsed, Pw = 10 ms single pulse), PD 200 mW for 2SC2412K (each terminal mounted on a reference land), Tj 150 degC.",
      "Guaranteed hFE bounds at IC = 1 mA, VCE = 6 V (min 120, max 560) are recorded as gain points with source_kind minimum/maximum and were not converted into typical values."
    ],
